{
  "id": "multitraitmultimethod-matrix",
  "term": "multitrait–multimethod matrix",
  "definition": "A multitrait–multimethod matrix is a research approach for analyzing how several traits or variables relate when they are measured using multiple methods or informants. In this context, it is used to separate the effects of who provides the information from the traits being studied and to test whether combining sources adds predictive value.",
